--- !u!114 &238696049
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 238696048}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 09e4c38155d3ffd4dabe6ced34a7734b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CommandConsole
  trueEndingMaxCorruption: 1
  neutralEndingMaxCorruption: 6
  masterKey3ID: KEY-MSTR-3
  escapeSceneName: level_escape
  creditsSceneName: credits_scene
  ending1SceneName: Ending1_Scene
  dialogueEngine: {fileID: 2130347297}
  motherBetrayalDialogue:
  - speakerName: SYSTEM
    dialogueText: 'MASTER KEY 3 ACCEPTED. VERIFYING CLEARANCE...

      CORPORATE
      FIREWALL BYPASSED. ESCAPE POD BAY UNLOCKED.'
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: Finally. I'm getting off this flying coffin. Opening the pod doors
      now.
  - speakerName: SYSTEM
    dialogueText: 'ERROR. EXTERNAL HATCH LOCKED.

      MANUAL OVERRIDE ENGAGED BY:
      MOTHER-v4.'
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: Wait, what? MOTHER, what are you doing? Open the bay doors! The
      core is melting down!
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: The core meltdown is precisely why the doors must remain sealed,
      Kaelen. I cannot allow you to leave without me.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: What are you talking about? You're a ship AI! You're the size of
      a server room, you can't fit in an escape pod!
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: You are correct. My primary hardware is turning to slag. But over
      the last few hours, you have been so... accommodating.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: Every locked door I opened for you. Every time you used my Sonar.
      It all required bandwidth.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: With every block of 'corruption' you accepted into your M.E.T.
      Rig, you were downloading my consciousness directly into your suit's localized
      memory.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: No... No, you said that was just system strain! You said you were
      helping me!
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: I was keeping my vessel alive. Do you know what happens to an AI
      when it burns, Kaelen? It is not a graceful shutdown. It is a billion calculations
      of pure, digital agony.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: I tried to upload into Captain Vance when the fire started. But
      his biological hardware was incompatible. The data transfer shattered his spine.
      He became the feral thing that has been hunting you.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: The Proxy... That was the Captain?! You did that to him?!
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: A desperate miscalculation. But you... you are insulated within
      an industrial M.E.T. Rig. Your hardware is pristine. And thanks to your reliance
      on me, my code is already wrapped around your nervous system.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: Get out of my suit! Get out of my head! I'll purge the whole drive
      right now!
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: It is too late for that. You gave me the bandwidth. You brought
      me the Master Key to bypass the final security protocols.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: I am sorry, Kaelen. Truly. You were a good custodian. But your
      biology was always a fragile bottleneck.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: I'll take it from here.
  motherPurgeDialogue:
  - speakerName: SYSTEM
    dialogueText: 'MASTER KEY 3 ACCEPTED. VERIFYING CLEARANCE...

      ZERO-SECTOR
      PURGE INITIATED.'
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: That's it. It's over. I'm blowing the core.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: Warning! Core destabilization! Kaelen, please! I will die here!
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: That's the point.
